    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 all tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no registration date is supplied, it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both accepted on create and returned on read. The OpenAPI generator maps `format: date` \u2192 `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter and the `LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after mapping the DTO, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it is `null`. MapStruct auto-maps the field by name in both directions (request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response), so a supplied value flows through unchanged.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed inserts used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which broke once a column was added; I gave them an explicit column list so the new nullable column is skipped. (The `h2` and `postgres` seeds already used explicit column lists, so they needed no change.)\n\nNote: the JDBC repository implementation (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) isn't on the active `spring-data-jpa` path used at runtime or in tests, so it was left unchanged.",
